IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra4-s105-recovery`

-- Tests for wra4-s105-recovery.l4 (s 105: SSAA 71ZB to 71ZH, 115B(4), SSA1998 Sch 3 paras 6A and 6B).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the Act, beside the assertion.

§ `fixtures`

`the payee` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "P1"
    `age in years` IS 40
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1985
    `where the person is` IS `England outside Greater London`
    `where the person lives` IS `England outside Greater London`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of payment`
GIVETH A Payment
`a payment of kind` MEANS Payment WITH
    `the kind of payment` IS k
    `the benefit paid` IS `universal credit`
    `the person it was paid to` IS `the payee`
    `the period paid for` IS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 28 1 2025
    `the amount paid for the period, in pounds` IS 400

§ `71ZB(1): paid in excess of entitlement`

-- Paid 500 against entitlement 400: 100 in excess. Paid 400 against 400: none. Paid 300 against 400: none.
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the amount paid in excess of entitlement` 500 400 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the amount paid in excess of entitlement` 400 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the amount paid in excess of entitlement` 300 400 EQUALS 0
-- Universal credit: not entitled (s 3) means nothing was due, so everything paid is in excess; entitled to 400 and paid 450 is 50.
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1)(a) the universal credit paid in excess of entitlement` FALSE 400 250 EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1)(a) the universal credit paid in excess of entitlement` TRUE 400 450 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1)(a) the universal credit paid in excess of entitlement` TRUE 400 400 EQUALS 0

§ `71ZB(1): the benefits whose overpayment may be recovered`

#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `universal credit` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `income-based jobseeker's allowance` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `contributory employment and support allowance` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `income-related employment and support allowance` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- housing credit, "except in prescribed circumstances"
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `housing credit` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `housing credit` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `housing credit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a benefit the list does not name: not covered (the grant is "any amount of the following")
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `income support` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `housing benefit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `council tax benefit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `child tax credit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `working tax credit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `state pension credit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `personal independence payment` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `disability living allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `industrial injuries benefit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `social fund payment` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `child benefit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `guardian's allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `bereavement allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `incapacity benefit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `maternity allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `severe disablement allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `widow's pension` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `widowed mother's allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` `widowed parent's allowance` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- membership of the list (a plain test)
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the benefit is named in the list` `housing credit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the benefit is named in the list` `universal credit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the benefit is named in the list` `income support` EQUALS FALSE

§ `71ZB(2) to (7)`

-- (2) recoverable from the person to whom it was paid, or such other person as may be prescribed
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) an amount paid in pursuance of a determination "is not recoverable ... unless" it was reversed, varied, revised or superseded
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) prescribed income paid late is the sole reason
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(5) the amount is treated as paid in excess of entitlement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(5) the amount is treated as paid in excess of entitlement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(5) the amount is treated as paid in excess of entitlement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) joint awards
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` `universal credit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` `universal credit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` `housing credit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` `income support` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7) the four ways
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` `deduction from benefit` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` `deduction from earnings` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` `court action` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` `adjustment of benefit` EQUALS TRUE

§ `71ZC deduction from benefit`

#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from this payment` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from this payment` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from this payment` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` TRUE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` TRUE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` TRUE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` TRUE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` TRUE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` FALSE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): a (2)(b) obligation is discharged "in prescribed circumstances"; (4): a (2)(c) obligation "in all cases"
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(4) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(4) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(4) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `71ZD deduction from earnings`

#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "earnings" has such meaning as may be prescribed: the regulations' answer when supplied
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) the person may be required to disclose details of their employer` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) the person may be required to disclose details of their employer` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) the person may be required to disclose details of their employer` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) the person may be required to disclose details of their employer` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(e) earnings must not be reduced below the level: earnings 1000, level 800: at most 200 may come off; at the level or below, nothing
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` 1000 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` 800 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` 700 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` 800.01 (JUST 800) EQUALS JUST 0.01
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` 1000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `71ZE court action`

-- England and Wales "if the county court so orders"; Scotland as an extract registered decree arbitral; elsewhere the section is silent
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `Greater London` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `Greater London` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `England outside Greater London` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `England outside Greater London` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` Wales TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` Wales FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` Scotland FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` Scotland TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `Northern Ireland` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` `outside the United Kingdom` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(3) the costs of recovery may be recovered as if recoverable under 71ZB` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZE(3) the costs of recovery may be recovered as if recoverable under 71ZB` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `71ZG payments on account`

#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(1) the Secretary of State may recover the payment` (`a payment of kind` `a payment on account`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(1) the Secretary of State may recover the payment` (`a payment of kind` `a payment of an award`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(1) the Secretary of State may recover the payment` (`a payment of kind` `a hardship payment`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(4) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(4) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` `deduction from benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` `deduction from earnings` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` `court action` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` `adjustment of benefit` EQUALS NOTHING

